From 0d2f9dce416a1553bc9fdef406e76706ef698f63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homelab-admin <homelab-admin@homelab>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:20:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] auth: accept /connect-spotify cookies whatever the
 account email

The trusted proxy decides who may use the app; the cookies decide whose
listening is tracked. In a one-user SSO deployment those are routinely
different accounts, and the old ownership check made the decoupling pointless:
mismatched cookies were refused, so nothing was ever recorded.

/connect-spotify now accepts the cookies, reads the Spotify profile, records
the reported email/display name on the user row and reports "Connected to
Spotify as <account>" with a way to replace the cookies. A failed profile read
is reported plainly and the cookies are still saved - tracking often works
even when the metadata call did not. The standalone login/register/reset
forms keep verifyCookiesForEmail: there the cookies ARE the credential, and
accepting a mismatched pair would hand one user's database to anyone who knew
their email. Trusted-header auth and its TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS peer check are
unchanged.
